---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Close from '../components/Close.astro';
---
<Base title="About Rachel" description="Rachel Glover is a Registered Clinical Counsellor (RCC) in Victoria, BC, working with couples, relationships and stepfamily dynamics.">
  <div class="wrap"><section class="pg-hero about-hero">
    <div class="copy">
      <p class="eyebrow rise" style="--d:.1s">About · Rachel Glover, RCC</p>
      <h1 class="b-h1"><span class="mask"><span style="--d:.2s">Hi, I’m</span></span><span class="mask acc"><span style="--d:.36s">Rachel.</span></span></h1>
      <div class="stack rise" style="--d:.65s">
        <p class="lede ink">I’m a Registered Clinical Counsellor (RCC) based in Victoria, BC, with a passion for working with couples, relationships and stepfamily dynamics.</p>
        <p class="lede">The relationships in our lives have a powerful influence on our happiness and well-being. As a wife, mother, stepmother and someone who deeply values strong friendships, I understand that relationships and family life take ongoing work, patience and a willingness to keep learning.</p>
        <p class="lede">I care a lot about the work I do. I bring warmth, honesty and curiosity to counselling, with a focus on getting to the heart of the issue and helping people make changes that carry into their everyday lives.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="photo about-photo slide-up rise" style="--d:.3s"><img src="/img/rachel-brick.jpg" alt="Rachel Glover, RCC, smiling, leaning against a brick wall" style="object-position:50% 6%" /></div>
  </section></div>

  <section class="band alt"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="reveal" style="max-width:760px"><p class="eyebrow">My approach</p><h2 class="b-h1 h2" style="margin-top:16px">Clinically, my work draws from several approaches.</h2></div>
    <div class="approach stagger">
      <div><h3>The Developmental Model of Couples Therapy</h3><p class="body">To understand how individuals and relationships grow and change over time.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Attachment Theory</h3><p class="body">To understand what brings us closer or creates distance.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Neuroscience</h3><p class="body">To understand what’s happening in the brain when we react the way we do.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="dev split2 reveal">
      <div class="stack"><p class="eyebrow">The Developmental Model</p><h3 class="b-h1" style="font-size:clamp(28px,3vw,40px)">Strong relationships grow as the people in them grow.</h3></div>
      <div class="stack">
        <p class="body">My approach to couples counselling is informed by the Developmental Model of Couples Therapy, developed by psychologists Dr. Ellyn Bader and Dr. Peter Pearson.</p>
        <p class="body">The model recognizes that relationships change and develop over time. As couples move through different stages of life, they encounter new challenges that require new skills and ways of relating to each other.</p>
        <p class="body">One of its central ideas is that a healthy relationship needs room for both individuals. You can be close, committed and supportive of one another while still having different needs, opinions and ways of seeing the world.</p>
        <p class="body">Rather than focusing only on what your partner needs to change, we also look at your own reactions, behaviours and contributions to the relationship. The goal is to help you become more confident in yourself, more understanding of each other and better equipped to grow together.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="band"><div class="wrap split2">
    <div class="reveal"><p class="eyebrow">How I work</p><h2 class="b-h1 h2">Warm, direct and <span class="acc">actively engaged.</span></h2></div>
    <div class="reveal stack">
      <p class="body">I take a warm yet direct approach to counselling. I am actively engaged in our sessions, asking thought-provoking questions, pointing out patterns and behaviours I notice, and bringing honesty with compassion about what I see.</p>
      <p class="body">We’ll get clear about what you want to change and keep our sessions focused on those goals. I’ll help you better understand what’s happening by sharing relevant research, relationship theory and, when helpful, real-life perspective. I’ll teach you useful skills and sometimes give suggestions to work on between sessions.</p>
      <p class="pull">I want you to leave counselling feeling relieved, equipped with new knowledge and hopeful about what can change.</p>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="band alt"><div class="wrap split2">
    <div class="reveal"><p class="eyebrow">Credentials</p><h2 class="b-h1 h2">Training and registration</h2></div>
    <div class="reveal"><ul class="creds">
      <li><span>Registered Clinical Counsellor (RCC)</span><span>BC Association of Clinical Counsellors</span></li>
      <li><span>Registration number</span><span class="todo">To confirm with Rachel</span></li>
      <li><span>Education</span><span class="todo">To confirm with Rachel</span></li>
      <li><span>Additional training</span><span class="todo">To confirm with Rachel</span></li>
    </ul></div>
  </div></section>

  <Close />
</Base>
